 "cv": "# Alex Rivera\n\nRemote · alex.rivera@example.com · +1 555 010 0199 · linkedin.com/in/alex-rivera-example · github.com/alex-rivera-example\n\n## Summary\n\nBackend engineer with seven years building payment and data platforms in TypeScript and Go. Comfortable owning a service from design review to on-call, and happiest where reliability work pays for itself in fewer incidents.\n\n## Core competencies\n\nDistributed Systems · API Design · PostgreSQL · Event-Driven Architecture · Observability · Kubernetes · TypeScript · Go\n\n## Experience\n\n### Senior Backend Engineer — Northwind Payments\n\nMarch 2022 - Present · Remote\n\n- Rebuilt the settlement pipeline as an event-driven service in Go, cutting end-of-day reconciliation from 4 hours to 25 minutes.\n- Led the move from cron jobs to a queue-backed scheduler with idempotent retries; payment-related incidents fell 60% in two quarters.\n- Introduced OpenTelemetry tracing across 14 services and wrote the runbooks the on-call rotation now uses.\n\n### Backend Engineer — Contoso Analytics\n\nJune 2019 - February 2022 · Austin, TX\n\n- Designed the public REST API for the reporting product (TypeScript, PostgreSQL), serving 3,000 customer integrations.\n- Cut p95 query latency from 1.8 s to 300 ms by reworking indexes and adding a read replica for heavy reports.\n- Mentored three junior engineers through their first production launches.\n\n### Software Engineer — Fabrikam Labs\n\nJuly 2017 - May 2019 · Austin, TX\n\n- Built internal tooling in Node.js for test-data generation, used by every QA team in the company.\n- Containerized the legacy monolith and wrote its first Kubernetes deployment manifests.\n\n## Projects\n\n### pg-shadow\n\nReplays production query traffic against a candidate schema to catch slow migrations before they ship. (Go, PostgreSQL)\n\nhttps://github.com/alex-rivera-example/pg-shadow\n\n## Education\n\n- B.S. Computer Science, University of Texas at Austin (2017)\n\n## Certifications\n\n- Certified Kubernetes Application Developer, CNCF, 2023\n\n## Skills\n\n- **Languages:** Go, TypeScript, SQL, Python\n- **Infrastructure:** Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, AWS\n- **Data:** PostgreSQL, Kafka, Redis\n"
